ode (e.g. `5263.KL` -> `Sunway Construction Group Berhad`). \n*Note: I have just updated the code to implement this, but the Streamlit server was killed by a system restart and needs to be restarted.*\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- The user is studying two trading books: \"海龟交易法则\" (Way of the Turtle) and \"Jack Investment\" (18岁开始的股票交易之路). \n- **Core Request:** \"can you create an apps that can screen the suitable malaysia and us stock in real time that i can buy and tell me my the TA and TP/CL and the entry price of the stock?\"\n- **Feature Request:** \"i want to put my buy price, then u do TPCL for me. as if this is able to tell me if its time to sell or not also\" (Implemented using an `@price` syntax, e.g. `SUNCON@2.50`).\n- **Feature Request:** \"can you show suggestion base on what i type? like this suncon? or can you process with the name i type straight?\" (Implemented using Yahoo Finance Search API).\n- **Latest Request:** \"put a remark on what is the status meaning? the sell signal the hold and stuff. and the ticker there, you still showing 5263.kl, whcih i dont know the number represent which stock\"\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- Located the two requested books in the user's `w:/My Drive/ZLibrary` workspace.\n- Extracted the trading strategies:\n  - **Jack Investment:** Swing trading using EMA 30, consolidation box breakouts, volume surges, and 1:1.5 Risk-Reward ratios.\n  - **Turtle Trading:** 20-day Donchian channel breakouts, entry - 2 ATR stop loss, 10-day low trailing exit.\n- Built a Streamlit web application (`stock_screener.py`) that fetches real-time data via `yfinance` and calculates signals for these two strategies.\n- Implemented smart ticker resolution using the Yahoo Finance Search API so the user can type \"SUNCON\" or \"APPLE\" and it automatically maps to the correct `.KL` or US ticker.\n- Implemented a custom entry price feature where the user can append `@price` (e.g. `SUNCON@2.50`) to track stocks they already own, dynamically generating HOLD / SELL / TAKE PROFIT signals.\n- Fixed pandas versioning bugs related to `yfinance` MultiIndex columns and the deprecation of `Styler.applymap`.\n- Added the requested status legend and full company name display to the code (just prior to server restart).\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Pandas V3 compatibility:** The `Styler.applymap()` method has been completely removed in Pandas 3.0+. You must use `Styler.map()` instead.\n- **yfinance MultiIndex:** Newer versions of `yfinance` return a MultiIndex for columns even when downloading a single ticker. This breaks standard Series calculations unless handled. The app handles this with:\n  ```python\n  if isinstance(df.columns, pd.MultiIndex):\n      df.columns = df.columns.droplevel(1)\n  ```\n- **Ticker Resolution:** The app uses `requests` to hit `https://query2.finance.yahoo.com/v1/finance/search?q={query}` to map shortnames to official tickers and full company names.\n- **Server Restart:** A system message indicated that all background tasks were killed. The Streamlit app is no longer running.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n- **Edited:** `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/stock_screener.py`\n  - This is the main application file. It contains functions to calculate indicators (`EMA30`, `ATR`, `Donchian`), analyze the Jack Investment strategy, analyze the Turtle strategy, and resolve tickers via Yahoo Finance. It uses Streamlit for the frontend.\n  - *Recent changes:* Added a Status Legend expander in the UI and updated the `resolve_ticker` function to return a `(ticker, shortname)` tuple so the final table displays the human-readable company name.\n\n- **Edited:** `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/implementation_plan.md` & `task.md`\n  - Created to outline and track the initial app architecture.\n\n- **Viewed:** `w:/My Drive/ZLibrary/02_To Read/2026/10_JACK INVESTMENT.pdf`\n  - Read entirely to extract the specific technical analysis rules used by the author (EMA 30, box theory, 2% risk, etc.) to encode into the app.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n- I have just updated `stock_screener.py` to include the status legend and the full company names in the results table, fulfilling the user's latest request.\n- However, the server restarted and the Streamlit background task was killed.\n- **Next Step:** You must restart the Streamlit server. Use `run_command` as a daemon to execute:\n  `python -m streamlit run stock_screener.py`\n  in the directory: `C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1`\n- **Next Step:** Send a message to the user letting them know that you have added the legend, updated the app to display full company names instead of just ticker codes, and that the app is back online at `http://localhost:8501`.\n\nYou have the 9 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787477117058]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/.tempmediaStorage/media_1787477117058.pdf\nLast Edited: 2026-08-23T09:25:17Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787478198912]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/.user_uploaded/media_1787478198912.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-23T09:43:19Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787478248613]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/.user_uploaded/media_1787478248613.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-23T09:44:09Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787478257179]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/.user_uploaded/media_1787478257179.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-23T09:44:17Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787479293517]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/wai_j/.gemini/antigravity/brain/c155f291-512d-4565-8630-f27b8bc949d1/.user_uploaded/media_1787479293517.png\nLast Edited: 2026-08-23T10:01:34Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1787479580104]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/wai_j/.g